// This service lives inside the Ecommerce monorepo, so it normally has NO
// go.mod of its own: the repository root is the single Go module
// (github.com/ecommerce) and Bazel owns the build. This file is only here for
// the case where a service must be extracted into its own repository.
//
// When extracted, add the platform capabilities it actually imports:
//
//	github.com/ecommerce/platform/observability/logging v0.1.0
//	github.com/ecommerce/platform/observability/metrics  v0.1.0
//	github.com/ecommerce/platform/observability/tracing  v0.1.0
//	github.com/ecommerce/platform/security/auth        v0.1.0
//	github.com/ecommerce/platform/security/secrets     v0.1.0
//
// Note that each capability is a separate module path: logging, metrics and
// tracing used to be one `platform/observability` package, which rules_go
// rejects because all three targets would resolve to the same Go import path.
